---
import Layout from '../../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Nav from '../../../components/Nav.astro';
import Footer from '../../../components/Footer.astro';
---

<Layout title="Self-hosting journey · Blog" description="Notes on getting the Liva compiler to compile itself, byte-identically.">
  <Nav />

  <main class="min-h-screen pt-32 pb-24">
    <article class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-6">
      <p class="section-num text-[color:var(--color-ink-3)] mb-4">
        <a href="/blog" class="hover:text-[color:var(--color-accent)] transition-colors">← blog</a>
      </p>

      <div class="font-mono-tight text-[12px] text-[color:var(--color-ink-3)] mb-3 uppercase tracking-wider">
        2026-04-12 · compiler · bootstrap
      </div>
      <h1 class="font-display text-4xl md:text-5xl tracking-tight leading-[1.05] mb-6">
        Notes on getting Liva to compile itself
      </h1>
      <p class="text-[color:var(--color-ink-2)] text-[17px] leading-relaxed mb-10">
        Phase 7 of the self-hosting plan closed in April. The compiler is now
        written entirely in Liva and produces a byte-identical binary across
        generations. Below: what broke, what worked, and what we’d skip
        next time.
      </p>

      <h2 class="font-display text-2xl tracking-tight mt-12 mb-4">The three generations test</h2>
      <p class="text-[15px] text-[color:var(--color-ink-2)] leading-relaxed mb-4">
        Self-hosting isn’t real until gen2 == gen3. Our CI runs:
      </p>
      <ol class="space-y-2 text-[15px] text-[color:var(--color-ink-2)] list-decimal pl-6 mb-6">
        <li>Compile the Liva sources of livac with the Rust-implemented bootstrap binary → <code class="px-1.5 py-0.5 bg-[color:var(--color-paper-2)] font-mono-tight text-[13px]">livac-gen1</code>.</li>
        <li>Use gen1 to compile its own Liva sources → <code class="px-1.5 py-0.5 bg-[color:var(--color-paper-2)] font-mono-tight text-[13px]">livac-gen2</code>.</li>
        <li>Use gen2 to compile the same sources again → <code class="px-1.5 py-0.5 bg-[color:var(--color-paper-2)] font-mono-tight text-[13px]">livac-gen3</code>.</li>
        <li><code class="px-1.5 py-0.5 bg-[color:var(--color-paper-2)] font-mono-tight text-[13px]">cmp livac-gen2 livac-gen3</code> must be byte-identical.</li>
      </ol>
      <p class="text-[15px] text-[color:var(--color-ink-2)] leading-relaxed mb-4">
        We didn’t get there on the first try. The first 16 gen2/gen3 diffs
        all came down to non-deterministic hash-map iteration leaking into
        codegen order. <code class="px-1.5 py-0.5 bg-[color:var(--color-paper-2)] font-mono-tight text-[13px]">IndexMap</code> everywhere fixed it.
      </p>

      <h2 class="font-display text-2xl tracking-tight mt-12 mb-4">What broke worst</h2>
      <ul class="space-y-3 text-[15px] text-[color:var(--color-ink-2)]">
        <li><strong>BS-FRAG</strong>: a class of bootstrap bugs where the bootstrap binary mishandled certain enum patterns the new compiler depended on. Fixed by pinning a known-good seed binary in <code class="px-1.5 py-0.5 bg-[color:var(--color-paper-2)] font-mono-tight text-[13px]">bootstrap/seed/</code>.</li>
        <li><strong>Recursive enums</strong>: needed implicit auto-boxing during codegen. We bootstrapped a manual <code class="px-1.5 py-0.5 bg-[color:var(--color-paper-2)] font-mono-tight text-[13px]">Box</code>-emitter first, then refactored once self-hosting closed.</li>
        <li><strong>Error trace chaining</strong>: surprisingly hard to express without exceptions. Landed as <code class="px-1.5 py-0.5 bg-[color:var(--color-paper-2)] font-mono-tight text-[13px]">or fail</code> with implicit cause linking.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2 class="font-display text-2xl tracking-tight mt-12 mb-4">What we’d skip</h2>
      <p class="text-[15px] text-[color:var(--color-ink-2)] leading-relaxed mb-4">
        We spent a sprint trying to keep the Rust-implemented compiler and
        the Liva-implemented compiler in sync feature-for-feature so we
        could switch back and forth. It wasn’t worth it. The Rust one is
        archived now and only exists to bootstrap from source.
      </p>

      <hr class="hairline my-12" />

      <div class="flex items-center justify-between font-mono-tight text-[13px]">
        <a href="/roadmap" class="text-[color:var(--color-ink-2)] hover:text-[color:var(--color-accent)] transition-colors">
          ← roadmap
        </a>
        <a href="https://github.com/liva-lang/livac" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="text-[color:var(--color-accent)] link-anim">
          source on GitHub →
        </a>
      </div>
    </article>
  </main>

  <Footer />
</Layout>
